+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling It Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted — amends [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) for NG-5
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined both changing and cancelling a visit once booked. The [2026-08-08 ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) confirmed the row as deliberate. It also required any later narrowing to be a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+A feature request on 2026-10-24 observed that visits "can currently only be created, never corrected". The owner decided at intake:
+
+> Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in. Record the narrowing the way the project records non-goal changes.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner's decision above.
+2. **Drop NG-5 entirely.** Rejected: the owner kept cancellation out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, under the same rules as booking. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope. A correction changes the visit itself and never adds a second one.
+
+A correction carries no lifecycle state, so the NG-5 rationale still holds for cancellation alone.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-5 now declines cancellation only. Its row records the narrowing.
+- `REQ-VIS-003` states the correction capability.
+- NG-4 is unchanged: no owner, pet, or visit is deleted.
+- The correction form gains no visible entry point in this request; the owner noted one may follow.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction requirement.
